            "block_content": "The following schedule for preventive care benefits is available to all employees and eligible retirees* enrolled in the Traditional Medical plan option. Also, for 2001, spouses of active employees continue to be eligible for a pap smear every other year from 35 to 49 and every year after 50, a baseline mammography between 35 and 40 and every two years thereafter, and a PSA test for males 50 years of age and over every year thereafter. Effective January 1, 2002, Medicare eligible retirees and dependents of active employees and dependents of retirees enrolled in the Traditional Medical Plan option are eligible for preventive care as outlined below.",
